00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.440
More importantly, APIs
are powering innovation.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.500
Companies using APIs
as a differentiator

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.650
and a competitive
advantage are winning.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:30.060
Take a look at something
like Uber Eats or Postmates.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:33.540
We have one application that
uses restaurant and menu

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:40.530
APIs, driver and delivery
APIs, payment APIs, all

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:44.350
in one seamless experience.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.940
From an enterprise
point of view,

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:49.870
APIs are essential for
creating innovative business

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:55.950
models and innovative modes
of engagement with customers.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:59.460
APIs have helped many businesses
meet customers' increasing

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.520
expectations for
connected experiences,

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.120
but they've also helped
some enterprises pursue

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.470
even bigger or more profound
business evolutions,

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:14.910
things such as unlocking new
revenue streams and product

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:17.940
categories, creating
online marketplaces,

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.730
executing platform
business models,

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.730
and even many of the
other things you'll

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.400
find in those much
loftier definitions

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.280
of digital transformation.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.030
Over the years, we've seen
this evolution happen.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:37.080
APIs started as a way
to improve access.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.400
REST as an alternative
to SOAP, HTTP

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.200
verbs with much
simpler architectures.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.440
We moved into an
integration model.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:54.240
Systems or software A connected
to system or software B,

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:58.060
sending and receiving data
between cloud systems.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:02.160
And today, many businesses
are still in this mindset.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.600
As enterprises have
become more mature,

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:12.370
they reach an experienced view
of APIs, mobile apps powered

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:16.510
by APIs that deliver
experiences to their customers,

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.300
like mobile check
deposits for your bank

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:24.190
or a loyalty rewards and payment
system for your favorite coffee

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.390
orders.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:29.410
But the enterprises that
truly unlock the power of APIs

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:34.820
reach this transformational
level, digital transformation

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:40.460
of the enterprise itself,
innovation, new revenue models,

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:45.660
improved partnerships, and
increased modes of engagement.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:49.230
From a long-standing
integration technology

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:52.740
to being a powerful
agent of transformation,

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.090
the evolution of APIs has
been impressive and exciting.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:01.320
Today, APIs are the
fundamental building blocks

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.540
for successful businesses.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.660
Yes, APIs.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.570
And for those of you who
don't know what an APIs is--

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:13.110
Application
Programming Interfaces.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:15.120
Application
programming interfaces

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.030
are helping companies
create the differentiators

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:21.510
for their products,
processes, and people.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.660
APIs are helping companies
innovate every day

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.460
to build new
connected experiences,

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:30.240
become more agile for customers,
and open up new business

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.610
markets to collaborate
with partners

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.730
and monetize their
digital assets.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:39.669
APIs are super powerful.

00:08:39.669 --> 00:08:41.990
But you know what?

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:45.070
The more I actually
think about it,

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:49.390
I personally don't agree
with this definition of APIs

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:50.800
anymore.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:55.730
Application
programming interface--

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:59.420
it sounds way too technical.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:02.660
And honestly, it doesn't
capture the essence

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.270
of meaningful and
continuous innovation

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.120
that we are talking about today.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:12.200
Maybe it's time for us to
actually innovate the API.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.640
If we are truly looking at
APIs to help drive our business

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:23.190
forward while also innovating
across products, processes,

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:26.340
and people, we should
probably start looking

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:29.070
at APIs in a different way.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:31.570
What if we change
things up a little bit?

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:37.340
Here's an option--
application product interface.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.760
Being able to build products
in new digital experiences

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.190
is essential for business today.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:47.300
A few weeks ago, I was having
this discussion on LinkedIn

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.130
with a group, and
the comment was

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:52.970
made that ignoring application
integration scenarios

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:57.980
means ignoring 98% of the
scenarios where APIs are

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:00.810
used in the real world today.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:05.180
Well, my response aligns with
how today's smart enterprises

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:07.910
need to think about APIs.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:12.560
I stated, no matter
what the integration is,

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:17.840
at the start of an API's life
is a value proposition that must

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:21.150
result in a business outcome.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:27.250
Otherwise, you wouldn't need the
integration in the first place.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:31.080
This is a complete
mindset shift.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.920
APIs are not just
about integration.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:38.670
APIs must be treated as
products no different

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:41.370
than any other
product you design,

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:44.760
build, or manage in
your organization.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.220
When you design
API products, you

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:52.370
should ask questions like what
problems do my users face?

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:57.200
How do I make the API
product easy to consume?

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.450
Do I start designing
API products

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:02.540
for an internal audience
or just jump right

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.970
into an external audience?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:09.080
Can proxies be reused in
multiple API products?

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:13.100
How can I measure the
impact of my API products?

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:16.850
The answers to these questions
will form your API product

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:21.470
strategy, and the strategy
must support your business.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:25.430
And you can manage your APIs,
as we were just talking about,

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:28.010
like other products
in your organization

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:30.560
with its own product lifecycle.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.310
Design your APIs from an
outside-in perspective.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:39.110
Document them so application
developers can innovate faster.

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:42.560
Market your APIs to
attract new opportunities,

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.410
allowing others to
help you innovate.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.440
And of course,
analyze what works

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:53.810
and what doesn't work so that
you can iterate on your APIs.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:56.620
And if you want to
get really crazy,

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:00.880
find ways to monetize
your new API products.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:04.060
There are numerous approaches,
such as revenue sharing,

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:06.850
fee-based models,
or even freemium,

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:10.300
allowing API consumers to play
with your APIs in a sandbox

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.470
before subscribing.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:16.160
Today, in hundreds of
organizations globally,

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:19.250
APIs have become the business.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:21.920
A great example
for monetization is

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:25.730
with AccuWeather, a global
leader in weather data.

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:30.380
AccuWeather wanted an easy way
to attract developers, monetize

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:35.810
data via flexible pricing plans,
and offer a seamless experience

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.390
that provides
customers the potential

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:41.910
to build the next big thing.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:43.800
Within the first two
months of going live

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:49.380
on the Apigee platform, nearly
2,500 experienced developers

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:54.330
paid for and accessed
APIs to innovate

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.820
new weather-based applications.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:13:02.790
And as of today, AccuWeather is
processing over 30 billion API

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.510
requests per day.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.450
Another example
of monetization is

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:09.900
with Swisscom, the
leading telecommunications

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:13.650
provider in Switzerland,
providing phone, internet,

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:16.890
and other services for
millions of customers.

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:19.260
Swisscom established
an API program

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.860
using Apigee to bridge
its network and resources

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.370
to outside apps and products.

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:31.470
As a result of their focus on
productization of their APIs,

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:35.730
Swisscom generates
millions in revenue

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:40.630
solely through their
Apigee API program.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:44.830
But maybe we can look
at APIs another way.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:49.780
How about application
process interface?

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:53.710
Streamlining innovation by
using a platform like Apigee

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:58.210
with tools that allows your
company to be more nimble

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:02.650
